Do the packed-int4 attention dots in fp16, not fp32.

This SM75 kernel does not use integer MMA, so it dequantized nibbles into fp32 and
fed fp32 dots, and the fp32 K/V tiles filled half of shared memory. The nibbles
are 0..15 and exactly representable in fp16, so the dots run in fp16 with fp32
accumulation while the zero-point corrections stay in fp32. Halves the tile
footprint; perplexity is unchanged.

Keep the int4 attention dequantized nibbles in the query dtype: they are
integers in [0, 15], exact in fp16, so the dots stay numerically identical
while using the fp16 tensor-core path (the fp32 path has no tensor cores on
sm75) and the K/V tiles halve -- which is what made the 64 KiB shared-memory
limit reject the multi-query 3D path (now boots and measures at parity with
the native path) and what any longer verify block would otherwise hit.

